 75ZN c  E(p)=1.4 GeV incident on UC{-x} target at ISOLDE-CERN                  
 75ZN2c  facility. Zn nuclei were resonantly ionized using a resonant           
 75ZN3c  laser-ion source, accelerated to 30 keV and mass separated.            
 75ZN4c  The ions were cooled using a gas-filled                                
 75ZN5c  radio-frequency quadrupole (RFQ-ISCOOL). Measured hyperfine spectra    
 75ZN6c  using collinear laser spectroscopy using COLLAPS setup at ISOLDE-CERN. 
 75ZN7c  Deduced changes in mean square charge radii relative to {+68}Zn.       
 75ZN8c  Systematic uncertainty are mainly from uncertainty on                  
 75ZN9c  atomic factors and F.                                                  
